# s2b-server-feed -> CORE-WIRE (G2)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml, [dependencies] (dependency edges only)

mixdog-app-server-client = { workspace = true }
mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
serde_json = { workspace = true }
tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros"] }

(mixdog-protocol is already listed: server_feed.rs uses mixdog_protocol::ThreadSummary.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml, [dev-dependencies] (new section)

async-trait = { workspace = true }
tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros"] }
mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }

(server_feed_tests.rs implements ProtocolClient over a scripted stub; it starts no cargo, binary or window. It uses no timer:
 no tokio::time call, so no test-support / virtual-clock feature is needed.)

## Module line

native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/src/lib.rs already declares `pub mod server_feed;`; nothing to add.
The test module is declared inside server_feed.rs (`#[cfg(test)] #[path = "server_feed_tests.rs"] mod tests;`).

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

None: this task registers no protocol service and consumes only methods that already exist
(thread/list, thread/finalAnswer/read, agent/pool/list, app/subscribe).

## Notes for the lead

- mixdog-workspace-hack: the new edges (tokio rt/sync/macros, serde_json, async-trait) are all features other crates already enable; run
  `cargo hakari generate` after applying.
